WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.868
-Last week, in a shocking
and sadly predictable move,

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:07.234
the Supreme Court overturned
Roe v Wade.

00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:09.400
I was angered,
saddened by the news.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.334
And before we get started,
I just want to be clear

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:14.601
that abortion
is not only a women's issue,

00:00:14.601 --> 00:00:16.367
it's not only
a pregnant person's issue.

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:18.133
It's everyone's issue.

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:21.033
We all benefit
from reproductive freedom

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:23.300
and from access to legal
and safe abortions.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.367
I think it's possible that men
hear, "My body, my choice,"

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:27.767
and we take away the message

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:30.000
that it's not our issue
to speak about,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.767
but it's everyone's job
to advocate

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:35.267
for reproductive rights.
So I asked my writers, Amber,

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:38.067
Jenny, and Ally,
what I can do to help

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:41.467
and they said,
"You can start by shutting up."

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:44.300
-That's right. We did.
-Okay.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.033
Okay.

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:49.567
Because, you know,
if something like this happens,

00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:52.200
we should center
the voices of people

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.133
who are most affected by it.

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:56.467
-We said to shut up.
-Okay.

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:58.934
-We are devastated
and disappointed

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:01.667
in our country right now.
We're joke writers,

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:03.567
but we didn't want
to come out here tonight

00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:06.968
and tell jokes or do goofy bits
that didn't feel right.

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:09.367
-Instead, we could
share our feelings.

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:13.067
-We could talk to an expert
on reproductive rights.

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:14.934
-Or we could burn it
all to the ground.

00:01:14.934 --> 00:01:18.400
-But -- But we're not going
to do that.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:19.901
We're going to do
the second one.

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:23.434
So please welcome the president
and CEO of Planned Parenthood

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:26.567
Federation of America,
Alexis McGill Johnson.

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:34.567
♪♪

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:42.534
♪♪

00:01:42.534 --> 00:01:44.267
-Alexis, thank you so much
for being here,

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:47.133
especially on today of all days.

00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:49.267
-Thank you so much
for having me.

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:50.834
Look, it's just not an honor.
I really appreciated

00:01:50.834 --> 00:01:54.033
your opening and saying that we
all have a stake in this fight,

00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:57.033
and I'm just grateful to be here
in this conversation with you.

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:59.067
-Alexis, we wanted to
ask you some questions.

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:02.501
First off, what does
this Supreme Court decision

00:02:02.501 --> 00:02:05.067
mean for Americans?

00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:07.934
-You know, what the
Supreme Court did on Friday

00:02:07.934 --> 00:02:10.767
is essentially tell us
that half the population

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:13.000
is not free and equal,
right?

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:19.200
26 states will be moving very
quickly in the next few weeks

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.434
to few months
to ban access to abortion

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:24.000
or severely restrict it,

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.100
meaning that if you live
in one state

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:29.300
like New York or California,
you will be free and equal.

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:33.567
And if you live in a state like
Texas or Oklahoma or Missouri,

00:02:33.567 --> 00:02:36.000
it may be that you won't
have access

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.100
to the care that you need.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.534
That would affect upwards
of 36 million people, right?

00:02:40.534 --> 00:02:41.634
And we've already seen
a little bit

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:42.801
of what that looks like,

00:02:42.801 --> 00:02:44.701
because we are living
in a post-Roe world

00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:46.801
in states like Texas
and Oklahoma.

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:49.534
We're seeing people
having to get in their cars

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:51.601
and drive thousands
of miles out of state

00:02:51.601 --> 00:02:53.834
just to get access to care.

00:02:53.834 --> 00:02:56.968
We are seeing people
who can't get out of state

00:02:56.968 --> 00:02:59.834
for many horrible reasons,

00:02:59.834 --> 00:03:03.067
and they're essentially
being forced into pregnancy.

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:07.033
And, you know, it just means
that, you know,

00:03:07.033 --> 00:03:09.334
that freedom is something --
it's a practice.

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:11.400
We have to continue to fight
for it over and over again.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.501
Yeah.

00:03:12.501 --> 00:03:15.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.167
-I've heard a lot of people say
that this ruling

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:25.100
is not just about abortion.
Can you explain what that means?

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.901
-Yeah, absolutely. It goes
far beyond abortion, right?

00:03:27.901 --> 00:03:29.701
I mean, you know,
first we have to ask, you know,

00:03:29.701 --> 00:03:31.334
in some of these states --
I don't know if you've seen

00:03:31.334 --> 00:03:33.234
kind of what the restrictions
look like, right?

00:03:33.234 --> 00:03:36.868
Some of them are banning access
to abortion after fertilization.

00:03:36.868 --> 00:03:39.934
You know, Texas has a six-week
ban, which is after -- you know,

00:03:39.934 --> 00:03:42.567
before actually many people
know that they are pregnant.

00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:46.100
But we've also seen
introductions of laws

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:47.367
in states like Missouri

00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:51.100
that are trying to ban moving
across state lines

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.934
to get access to care.

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:57.501
We've seen states like Louisiana
that are banning access to IVF

00:03:57.501 --> 00:04:01.701
and IUDs
and emergency contraception,

00:04:01.701 --> 00:04:04.033
Plan B, right?
They're introducing these laws

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:07.000
that are so incredibly,
you know, extreme.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.901
And so when we talk about
the kind of notion of like,

00:04:09.901 --> 00:04:11.767
this is just about abortion,

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:14.734
it is really about control
over our own bodies.

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:16.701
When you look
at the way the law --

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:19.100
the opinions are written,

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.467
you know, there are also
kind of indications

00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:22.901
that there are
other opportunities to go

00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:25.300
after things
like marriage equality,

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:27.367
like interracial marriage,

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:29.200
you know, like access
to contraception,

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.200
all of which has enjoyed
federal protections

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.767
as well, constitutional
protections.

00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:34.467
And that's where we really need
to be concerned

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:36.300
of overreach here.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:40.367
-So what are you hearing
from your patients right now?

00:04:40.367 --> 00:04:41.968
-Just devastation, right?

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:43.801
I mean, the ruling
came down on Friday

00:04:43.801 --> 00:04:45.968
when we had patients who were,

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:48.200
you know,
making their way to the clinic.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:49.934
And, you know, we all thought
that the decision

00:04:49.934 --> 00:04:51.767
would come down
sometime this week, right?

00:04:51.767 --> 00:04:53.601
Which would be
the full end of the term,

00:04:53.601 --> 00:04:55.734
which meant that we were rushing
to get as many patients in

00:04:55.734 --> 00:04:57.467
to be seen as possible.

00:04:57.467 --> 00:05:00.300
They are scared.
They are confused.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.701
They are worried
about criminalization

00:05:02.701 --> 00:05:04.767
because we don't know
what the other spate of laws

00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:06.234
is going to look like, right?

00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:08.067
We don't know
how they're going to enforce

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:10.701
the other abortion bans

00:05:10.701 --> 00:05:14.801
that they are going
to put in place.

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:17.067
And they're concerned, you know.
Most people who seek access

00:05:17.067 --> 00:05:18.868
to abortion care
are already parents,

00:05:18.868 --> 00:05:20.634
so they're worried about,
you know,

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:22.067
how to take care
of their families

00:05:22.067 --> 00:05:25.200
and how to ensure that they have
what they need to move forward

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.667
for their own,
you know, self-determination.

00:05:27.667 --> 00:05:30.367
So, you know,
we're trying to reassure them.

00:05:30.367 --> 00:05:34.601
There is a website
called AbortionFinder.org

00:05:34.601 --> 00:05:36.033
that we have, you know,

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:38.033
connected to with
an organization called

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:41.567
Power To Decide, where people
can find access to appointments.

00:05:41.567 --> 00:05:45.968
But the reality is,
you know, 24 states,

00:05:45.968 --> 00:05:49.234
you know, just can't absorb
the nation's care, right?

00:05:49.234 --> 00:05:54.167
So we're looking at a health
care crisis coming upon us.

00:05:54.167 --> 00:05:58.200
-Alexis, what role does sex
education play in all of this?

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.634
-Oh, I mean, sex education
is everything, right?

00:06:00.634 --> 00:06:02.901
I mean, in order
to control your body,

00:06:02.901 --> 00:06:04.400
you have to understand
how it works. Right?

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:07.400
In order to advocate
for your body and your freedoms,

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.968
you have to understand kind of

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:11.400
how your body works
and what that looks like.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:12.834
I think it's one
of the many tools

00:06:12.834 --> 00:06:16.834
that we have to essentially
raise this next new generation

00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:19.534
to understand
kind of what's at stake.

00:06:19.534 --> 00:06:22.167
The states that don't
teach sex ed, for example --

00:06:22.167 --> 00:06:25.067
the states that are
abstinence-only -- are states

00:06:25.067 --> 00:06:27.567
where we see higher rates
of unintended pregnancies

00:06:27.567 --> 00:06:29.400
because of course, people don't
know how to control them, right?

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:31.234
So I think that all of the ways

00:06:31.234 --> 00:06:33.534
in which we think
about how our bodies,

00:06:33.534 --> 00:06:35.267
how our gender,
how our sexuality,

00:06:35.267 --> 00:06:38.834
how our race intersects with
our kind of our own advocacy

00:06:38.834 --> 00:06:40.767
is the opportunity
that we have to kind of raise

00:06:40.767 --> 00:06:42.501
a new, different generation.

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:44.968
-So I have a question
from the perspective of men,

00:06:44.968 --> 00:06:48.033
and I know there are many of us
who support this issue.

00:06:48.033 --> 00:06:51.601
We aren't exactly sure
the best way to show it --

00:06:51.601 --> 00:06:53.200
how -- what is the best,

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:56.467
the most effective way to show
that we're allies in this fight?

00:06:56.467 --> 00:06:58.667
-Well, look, a good ally
is an active ally,

00:06:58.667 --> 00:07:01.701
not a passive ally, right?
You're a great ally right now,

00:07:01.701 --> 00:07:03.567
kind of centering
this conversation

00:07:03.567 --> 00:07:04.901
as the opening of the show.

00:07:04.901 --> 00:07:07.234
And it's important
for men to talk about

00:07:07.234 --> 00:07:09.300
what's happening
and what's at stake, right?

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:14.300
You're, you know, also affected
by the impact to abortion.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:17.901
You're also hurt by patriarchy.
You're also hurt by misogyny.

00:07:17.901 --> 00:07:19.434
And I think it's kind
of actually sexy

00:07:19.434 --> 00:07:21.000
when people support
reproductive rights.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.701
I don't know about you.

00:07:22.701 --> 00:07:25.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:28.501 --> 00:07:33.667
-So we've all had a few days
to be very, very angry now.

00:07:33.667 --> 00:07:36.567
And I -- But if we want to move
from anger to action,

00:07:36.567 --> 00:07:38.367
what can we do?

00:07:38.367 --> 00:07:39.767
-Well, look,
I think we all started off

00:07:39.767 --> 00:07:43.400
incredibly sad and devastated,
and that devastation

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:46.734
turned very quickly
into that rage,

00:07:46.734 --> 00:07:50.868
right, where we have to channel
that right now into action.

00:07:50.868 --> 00:07:54.033
It is really important right now
if you want to care for patients

00:07:54.033 --> 00:07:55.434
and get patients to care,

00:07:55.434 --> 00:07:57.601
support your local
Planned Parenthood organization.

00:07:57.601 --> 00:08:00.100
Support independent clinics
in those states

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:04.167
that are going to see
abortion bans be restricted --

00:08:04.167 --> 00:08:05.467
abortion be restricted.

00:08:05.467 --> 00:08:08.267
You can go to KeepOurClinics.org
to support them.

00:08:08.267 --> 00:08:11.067
You can go to AbortionFunds.org,

00:08:11.067 --> 00:08:13.367
which are resources
that help get patients --

00:08:13.367 --> 00:08:15.067
you know, it's travel money,
gas money.

00:08:15.067 --> 00:08:17.834
You know, just to get out of
state is critically important.

00:08:17.834 --> 00:08:21.100
You can share
about your fight for access

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.334
by going to #BansOffOurBodies

00:08:23.334 --> 00:08:25.601
to find places
that will be a place

00:08:25.601 --> 00:08:28.000
to update you around all of
the things that are going on.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:30.767
And then of course, you can
share your own stories,

00:08:30.767 --> 00:08:32.400
right, at #WhateverTheReason,

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:35.467
because part of why this
conversation is so important

00:08:35.467 --> 00:08:37.133
is because of stigma, right?

00:08:37.133 --> 00:08:39.767
We are here
because we have stigmatized

00:08:39.767 --> 00:08:41.100
a very normal procedure,

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:42.601
one that one in four women
in their life

00:08:42.601 --> 00:08:44.367
will have an abortion,

00:08:44.367 --> 00:08:45.767
and the fact that we have
stigmatized --

00:08:45.767 --> 00:08:47.767
the fact that we don't talk
about it means

00:08:47.767 --> 00:08:51.868
that people can make policies
that codify our inequality.

00:08:51.868 --> 00:08:54.434
And if we want to stay free, we
have to talk about our freedom

00:08:54.434 --> 00:08:56.868
and we have to ensure
that people understand

00:08:56.868 --> 00:08:59.534
what is critically
important here.

00:08:59.534 --> 00:09:01.434
-Alexis, we cannot
thank you enough

00:09:01.434 --> 00:09:03.000
for being with us here tonight.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.367
I also want to thank Amber,
Jenny, and Ally

00:09:05.367 --> 00:09:07.067
for being here
and helping us out.

00:09:07.067 --> 00:09:09.434
And we're going to be right back
with more "Late Night."

00:09:09.434 --> 00:09:10.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

